  "notes": "USAGE: {報告|ほうこく} is commonly used in business and official contexts for formal reporting.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{報告|ほうこく}する (to report)\n・{報告|ほうこく}を{受|う}ける (to receive a report)\n・{報告書|ほうこくしょ} (written report)\n・{報告|ほうこく}{会|かい} (report meeting)\n・{進捗|しんちょく}{報告|ほうこく} (progress report)\n・{中間|ちゅうかん}{報告|ほうこく} (interim report)\n\nBUSINESS NOTE: In Japanese workplaces, ほうれんそう ({報告|ほうこく}・{連絡|れんらく}・{相談|そうだん}) is an important concept emphasizing reporting, communication, and consultation.",
